$$
\frac{1}{9} = 1 - \left(\frac{1}{2}x + \frac{1}{3}y + z\right)
$$

Then,

$$
\left(\frac{1}{2}x + \frac{1}{3}y + z\right) = 1 - \frac{1}{9} = \frac{8}{9}
$$

So,

$$
\frac{1}{2}x + \frac{1}{3}y + z = \frac{8}{9} \tag{1}
$$

We also have from before:

$$
x + y + z = 18 \tag{2}
$$

